  "reason": "With no prior experiments, there is complete uncertainty about the performance landscape across all design dimensions (modality, encoder, profile type, aggregation, fusion). The most informative first experiment is a clean, minimal baseline: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000). This establishes the RNA-only performance floor using the most standard and computationally straightforward encoder (PCA) with the simplest profile setting. It serves as a reference point against which all subsequent experiments can be compared—whether multiprofile aggregation helps, whether learned encoders (scvi, scgpt) outperform PCA, whether image modality adds value, and whether multimodal fusion improves over unimodal baselines. Starting from the simplest configuration minimizes confounding factors and ensures that any future performance change can be attributed to a specific design decision rather than compounding complexity."
}

